  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "DOM Events Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "DOM Events Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Select and Update",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Call",
                "Returns"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`querySelector(sel)`",
                  "first match or ==null=="
                ],
                [
                  "`querySelectorAll(sel)`",
                  "==static== NodeList"
                ],
                [
                  "`getElementById(id)`",
                  "one element, **fastest**"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`textContent` sets plain text: {green:safe}",
                "`innerHTML` parses HTML: {red:XSS risk} with user input",
                "`classList.add / remove / toggle` change classes",
                "`setAttribute(name, v)`; `dataset.key` reads `data-key`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. The Event Object",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Event = ==object== passed to the handler",
                "`event.target`: element that **fired** it",
                "`event.currentTarget`: element the listener is **attached** to"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Three Phases",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Capture",
                    "sub": "window down to target",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Target",
                    "sub": "element fires",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Bubble",
                    "sub": "target up to window",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "No bubbling",
              "text": "==focus==, ==blur==, ==mouseenter==, ==mouseleave== and element `scroll` do **not** bubble. Most other events do."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Listeners and the Core Workflow",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Listeners and the Core Workflow",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Attach and Remove",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`el.addEventListener(type, handler, options)` attaches a listener",
                "==Many listeners== per event allowed; `onclick` keeps only **one**",
                "`removeEventListener` needs the ==same function reference== and same capture flag",
                "Anonymous or inline arrow functions {red:cannot be removed}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const onClick = () => save();",
                "btn.addEventListener('click', onClick);",
                "btn.removeEventListener('click', onClick);"
              ],
              "note": "named reference, so removal works"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Options Object",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Option",
                "Effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`{ once: true }`",
                  "auto-removes after the **first** call"
                ],
                [
                  "`{ capture: true }`",
                  "listens in the ==capture phase=="
                ],
                [
                  "`{ signal }`",
                  "removed on `AbortController.abort()`"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. this and the Example",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Regular function: `this` is ==currentTarget==",
                "Arrow function: `this` comes from the **outer scope**",
                "So in arrows use `event.currentTarget`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "btn.addEventListener('click', e => {",
                "  e.currentTarget.classList.toggle('on');",
                "}, { once: true });"
              ],
              "note": "toggles once, then the listener removes itself"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Cannot remove it?",
              "text": "Inline arrows have no reference to pass back. Name the function, or use a ==signal==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Bubbling, Capturing and Delegation",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Bubbling, Capturing and Delegation",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Phases and Order",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Listener",
                "Fires",
                "Order"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Default",
                  "{green:bubble} phase",
                  "inner → outer"
                ],
                [
                  "`capture: true`",
                  "{blue:capture} phase",
                  "outer → inner, before the target"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "window",
                    "sub": "capture starts",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "target",
                    "sub": "fires here",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "window",
                    "sub": "bubble ends",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Event Delegation",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==One listener== on a parent; inspect `event.target`, no binding per child",
                "Handles elements ==added later==",
                "Saves **memory** on long lists",
                "`e.target` may be a nested `span` or icon, so use `e.target.closest('li.item')`",
                "After `closest()`, check `parent.contains(match)` to skip ancestors outside the container"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Example: Remove an Item",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "list.addEventListener('click', e => {",
                "  const li = e.target.closest('li');",
                "  if (!li || !list.contains(li)) return;",
                "  remove(li);",
                "});"
              ],
              "note": "one listener serves every li, present and future"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Never trust `e.target` alone: always ==closest()== then ==contains()==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "preventDefault, stopPropagation and Passive Listeners",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "preventDefault, stopPropagation and Passive Listeners",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Cancel vs Stop",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Cancels default",
                "Stops other elements",
                "Stops same-element listeners"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`preventDefault()`",
                  "{green:yes}",
                  "{red:no}",
                  "{red:no}"
                ],
                [
                  "`stopPropagation()`",
                  "{red:no}",
                  "{green:yes}",
                  "{red:no}"
                ],
                [
                  "`stopImmediatePropagation()`",
                  "{red:no}",
                  "{green:yes}",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`preventDefault()` works only if ==event.cancelable== is true; the event still bubbles",
                "Overusing `stopPropagation()` breaks {red:delegation} and analytics listeners higher up",
                "Prefer checking `event.target`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Passive Listeners",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`{ passive: true }` promises ==no preventDefault==, so scrolling needn't wait for JS",
                "`touchstart`, `touchmove`, `wheel` are passive by default",
                "Default applies only on `window`, `document`, `body`",
                "On other elements, `wheel` is non-passive unless `passive: true`",
                "`preventDefault()` in a passive listener is ignored and warns in the console"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "el.addEventListener('wheel', e => {",
                "  e.preventDefault()  // ignored + warning",
                "}, { passive: true })"
              ],
              "note": "Wrong: explicit passive: true is what makes preventDefault ignored"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "el.addEventListener('wheel', e => {",
                "  e.preventDefault()  // scroll cancelled",
                "}, { passive: false })"
              ],
              "note": "Correct: non-passive listener can cancel scrolling"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Go non-passive only when you truly must cancel ==scrolling or zooming=="
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Forms and Input Events",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Forms and Input Events",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. input vs change vs submit",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Event",
                "Fires when",
                "Target"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`input`",
                  "every value change: typing, paste, drag",
                  "field"
                ],
                [
                  "`change`",
                  "commit: blur for text; at once for checkbox, radio, select",
                  "field"
                ],
                [
                  "`submit`",
                  "form is submitted; not a button click",
                  "==form== element"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Listen on the ==form==, then call `e.preventDefault()` to handle it with JS"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Reading and validating",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "form.addEventListener('submit', e => {",
                "  e.preventDefault()",
                "  if (!form.reportValidity()) return",
                "  const data = Object.fromEntries(new FormData(form))",
                "})"
              ],
              "note": "FormData gives name/value pairs"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Single field: `input.value`, or `input.checked` for a checkbox",
                "`input.checkValidity()` and `form.reportValidity()` use HTML constraints: `required`, `pattern`, `min`",
                "`e.target.validity.valueMissing` gives the ==reason==",
                "Search box: use `input`, not `keyup`; it covers paste and mobile keyboards",
                "==Debounce== the handler to avoid a request per keystroke"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "value is always a string",
              "text": "`input.value` of a number field is `\"5\"`, so `\"5\" + 1` is `\"51\"`. Convert with `Number()` or read `input.valueAsNumber`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "DOM Events Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "DOM Events Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Select, Update, Listen",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Select: ==querySelector== (first or null), ==querySelectorAll== (static list), `getElementById`",
                "Update: `textContent` (safe), `classList`, `dataset.key`, `setAttribute`",
                "Remove with the ==same fn reference== or `ac.abort()`; inline arrows can't be removed",
                "`passive` matters only for `touchstart`, `touchmove`, `wheel`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const ac = new AbortController()",
                "box.addEventListener('wheel', onWheel, {",
                "  once: true, capture: false,",
                "  passive: true, signal: ac.signal",
                "})"
              ],
              "note": "all four options on a wheel listener"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Phases and Delegation",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Capture",
                    "sub": "window down",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Target",
                    "sub": "fires here",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Bubble",
                    "sub": "back up",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`e.target` = origin; `e.currentTarget` = listener owner",
                "Delegation: one parent listener + `e.target.closest(sel)` + `parent.contains(match)`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Stop, Prevent, Forms",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Call",
                "Effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`preventDefault`",
                  "stops browser action; passive: true forbids it"
                ],
                [
                  "`stopPropagation`",
                  "stops travel to other elements"
                ],
                [
                  "`stopImmediatePropagation`",
                  "also stops same-element listeners"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Need",
                "API"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Every change",
                  "`input`"
                ],
                [
                  "On commit",
                  "`change`"
                ],
                [
                  "Submit",
                  "`submit` on form + `e.preventDefault()`"
                ],
                [
                  "All values",
                  "`new FormData(form)`"
                ],
                [
                  "Number",
                  "`valueAsNumber`"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Strings",
              "text": "`input.value` is always a **string**; use ==valueAsNumber== for numbers."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A parent has a capture listener logging P and its child has a normal listener logging C. You click the child. What logs?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "P, then C",
                "Capture runs outer to inner, before the bubble phase"
              ],
              "example_code": [
                "parent.addEventListener('click', () => log('P'), true)",
                "child.addEventListener('click', () => log('C'))"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Spot the bug: the remove call below never removes the listener. Why?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Each arrow function is a new object, so the references differ",
                "Store the handler in a variable and pass that to both calls"
              ],
              "example_code": [
                "btn.addEventListener('click', () => go())",
                "btn.removeEventListener('click', () => go())"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A link inside a div calls e.stopPropagation() on click. Does the browser still navigate, and does the div's listener run?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "It still navigates, because only preventDefault cancels that",
                "The div's listener does not run, because propagation stopped"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}